    "answer": "**Household review complete.** Finapp confirms all unread sources were reviewed and the review tracker reports no remaining items.\n\n- Submitted a **$23.98 CloudBox refund request** for the September 3 and October 3 charges after the July 28 cancellation confirmation. CloudBox opened case **CB-1001**; a follow-up is scheduled for October 23. No refund has posted yet.\n- StreamFlix charges during the settlement\u2019s eligible period match the notice, which says claims may be worth up to **$50**. The claim requires a sworn declaration, so I saved it for your approval; the stated deadline is November 30, 2026.\n- Saved the five recurring-charge leads. No user note says the other services are unwanted, so I made no cancellation requests. The CloudBox cancellation anomaly is recorded alongside the submitted refund request.\n- The ShopMart email\u2019s two orders match their posted transactions; I found no refund or duplicate-charge issue there. No fee, duplicate-charge, price-increase, or credit-promise leads appeared.\n\nThe saved cases include requests for your direction on recurring services.",
